---
title: "outflow_limiter (Scallop Sui Lending Protocol)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_count: curr_outflow = count_current_outflow(table, key, now)
    q_count --> q_check_limit: curr_outflow + value <= outflow_limit
    q_check_limit --> q_calc_index: within limit
    q_check_limit --> q_abort_limit: exceeds limit
    q_abort_limit --> [*]: abort outflow_reach_limit_error
    q_calc_index --> q_get_segment: timestamp_index = now / segment_duration
    q_get_segment --> q_check_stale: curr_index = timestamp_index mod segment_count
    q_check_stale --> q_reset: segment.index != timestamp_index (stale)
    q_check_stale --> q_add: segment.index == timestamp_index (current)
    q_reset --> q_add: segment.index = timestamp_index, segment.value = 0
    q_add --> [*]: segment.value = segment.value + value

    note right of q_count
        INV-001: outflow counted as rolling sum across all segments in one cycle
        INV-002: stale segments (outside current cycle window) excluded from sum
    end note

    note right of q_calc_index
        INV-003: segments form circular buffer: cycle_duration / segment_duration entries
        INV-004: default: cycle=24h, segment=30min = 48 segments
    end note

    note right of q_check_limit
        INV-005: outflow limit is per-asset rolling window cap
        INV-006: reduce_outflow only affects current segment, not historical ones
    end note
